menu "Wake word detector"

config WAKE_WORD_THRESHOLD_PCT
    int "Wake word confidence threshold (%)"
    range 0 100
    default 95
    help
        Fire only when the hey_hotpin class score reaches this percentage.
        Measured on the bench: real phrases land at 0.92-0.996, ordinary
        speech peaks near 0.50, and a quiet room stays under 0.05. 95 keeps
        every real detection while leaving a wide false-accept margin.

config WAKE_WORD_SELFTEST
    bool "Run inference self test at boot"
    default y
    help
        Runs a few inferences on a synthetic window at startup and logs the
        MFCC and neural network timing. Validates the deployment without a
        microphone attached.

endmenu

menu "INMP441 microphone"

config MIC_BCLK_GPIO
    int "I2S bit clock GPIO"
    range 0 39
    default 14
    help
        WARNING: GPIO2/4/12/13/14/15 are the SPI flash bus on an ESP32-CAM.
        Using them makes the I2S peripheral and the flash controller drive the
        same pads. This build deliberately uses 14/15/13 to test the user's
        existing wiring; expect instability if flash is also accessed.

config MIC_WS_GPIO
    int "I2S word select GPIO"
    range 0 39
    default 15

config MIC_DIN_GPIO
    int "I2S data-in GPIO"
    range 0 39
    default 13

config MIC_GAIN_SHIFT
    int "Microphone right-shift (lower = louder)"
    range 0 20
    default 11
    help
        The INMP441's 24-bit payload sits in bits 31..8 of the 32-bit I2S slot.
        14 was far too quiet - the detector only fired at arm's length. 10 added
        about 24 dB but saturated at 32768. 11 is the current setting. Watch the
        "audio peak" figure in the PEAK log line: keep speech peaks near
        8000-25000, raise the number if it pins at 32768, lower it if it stays
        under 3000.

config STATUS_LED_GPIO
    int "Status LED GPIO (-1 to disable)"
    range -1 39
    default 4
    help
        GPIO4 drives the AI-Thinker ESP32-CAM on-board LED (active low). It is
        also SPI flash SD1, which is only driven in QIO mode. This build runs
        the flash in DIO, so the pin is free at runtime - do not switch back to
        QIO while this LED is enabled.

config STATUS_LED_ON_MS
    int "Status LED on time after a trigger (ms)"
    range 50 5000
    default 250

endmenu
